  body: "# Unknown earnings and unreceived earnings in chapter 15\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe
    source distinguishes a reasonable assessment where the amount of earnings is unknown from treating
    unpaid or low-paid services as notional earnings; it records a 2002 ruling against the latter provision
    in this chapter.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nDMG 15015–15016 describe a particular regulation and
    retain a separate minimum-wage qualification. Neither a current minimum-wage rate nor current legal
    effects are established. The exclusion of JSA and IS in DMG 15000 means their chapter 26 notional-earnings
    provisions cannot simply be imported here.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 15000, PDF page
    2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a04ed307d7bff3604d6dc3/dmgch15.pdf#page=2) — DMG
    Vol 3: Ch 15: Earnings for non-income-related benefits.\n- [DMG 15014, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a04ed307d7bff3604d6dc3/dmgch15.pdf#page=5)
    — DMG Vol 3: Ch 15: Earnings for non-income-related benefits.\n- [DMG 15015, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a04ed307d7bff3604d6dc3/dmgch15.pdf#page=5)
    — DMG Vol 3: Ch 15: Earnings for non-income-related benefits.\n- [DMG 15016, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a04ed307d7bff3604d6dc3/dmgch15.pdf#page=5)
    — DMG Vol 3: Ch 15: Earnings for non-income-related benefits.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\n\
    Model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot.
    Specialist review is required. Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this
    record’s authoring time are separate.\n\nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official
    DWP document, individual advice, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted
    text may alter reading order, footnotes and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage
    or behavioural evaluation pass is claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol3-ch15`: PDF SHA-256 `b9a278572b8205196c4b0c2d1b0c3c8032dddff62587e3ba0ff7fc897c670e4e`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `37d8db04ba2cd204591b67e3f3d8099a4c96be8f86ee788c70ab275322060a70`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/jsais-notional-employed-earnings
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The chapter explicitly excludes JSA and IS and records a different notional-earnings
      limitation; this association flags a regime boundary, not equivalence or incorporation of
      chapter 26.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch15/0002
      quote: "15000 The guidance in this chapter concerns the calculation of the weekly amount of earnings
        of\nemployed earners and self-employed earners for the purposes of\n\n\n1. benefits under certain
        legislation (for example IB) 1\n\n\n2. the exempt work provision for IfW2\n\n\n3. CA\n\n\n4. ADI
        and CDI.\n\n\nNote: This chapter does not provide guidance for UC, JSA, IS, ESA or SPC. For guidance
        on earnings for\nthose benefits please refer to the relevant chapters of the DMG and ADM.\n\n\n\
        \                                       1 SS CB Act 92 Parts II - V; SS Ben (C of E) Regs, reg
        3(1); 2 R(IB) 1/06"
      locator: DMG 15000
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch15/0005
      quote: "15015 On 11.11.02 a Commissioner decided1 that the regulation2 which permits a DM to take
        into account\nnotional earnings where a person is working for nothing or for less than that paid
        for comparable\nemployment in the area was ultra vires.\n\n\n                                \
        \                              1 R(IB) 7/03; 2 SS Ben (C of E) Regs, reg 4(2)"
      locator: DMG 15015
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch15/0005
      quote: "15016 This means that, in these circumstances, a claimant cannot be treated as possessing
        earnings\nwhich that person does not in fact possess. As the notional earnings provisions are
        not available DMs\nshould consider the NMW Provisions. See DMG 15017 - 15019.\n\n\n\n\nNational
        minimum wage"
      locator: DMG 15016
